proofs.proof_tex:
By the attained-interval theorem and \(A>0\),
\[
\operatorname{length}\{\Theta(P)\}
=\frac{T-V_P^-}{A}-\frac{T-V_P^+}{A}
=\frac{V_P^+-V_P^-}{A}
=\frac{R(P)}{A}.
\]
The nonempty identified interval is a singleton exactly when this length is zero, which is equivalent to \(V_P^+=V_P^-\), and the definition of \(R(P)\) makes this equivalent to \(R(P)=0\).
